  "title": "The top hole bit closes the decoder route",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "For the binary left-pigeon principle with n = 2^l holes and n + 1 pigeons, whose hole rows carry l + 1 bits, only pigeon n has the top code bit, so the reduced decoder sends the top bit of hole row h to the single cell X_n,h and every row-linear monomial with top bits on two different hole rows to zero: these monomials lie in the decoder's kernel K_k. Consequently every subspace of L_k that meets K_k only in zero has dimension at most low_k, the number of row-linear monomials of degree <= k with at most one top hole bit, and Braun's criterion applied through Theorem (R) certifies at most 3S + |J| >= 5.2, for every degree k <= n/2 and every accuracy h that Theorem (R) allows. The obstruction comes from the extra pigeon: the left-pigeon principle with 2n pigeons, whose codes fill the l + 1 bits, does not have it.",
  "dependencies": [
    "HOLE-SEP-20261110-001A",
    "SEP-LEFT-20261110-001A"
  ],
